@node Terminology
@section Terminology

@cindex terminology
@cindex glossary
These are the words the rest of the manual uses; each is defined once
here and used the same way everywhere.

@cindex city
@cindex host
@cindex rig
@cindex agent
@cindex session
@cindex polecat
@cindex bead
@cindex convoy
@cindex order
@cindex sling
@cindex formula
@cindex run
@cindex step
@cindex store
@cindex view
@table @dfn
@item city
A Gas City workspace rooted at a @file{city.toml}, with one supervisor
and one @command{gc} control plane.  Every view belongs to exactly one
city.
@item host
The machine a city runs on.  A local host is reached directly; a remote
host is reached over TRAMP and ssh (@pxref{Remote Cities}).
@item rig
A repository inside a city that owns a beads store and runs its own pool
of agents.  A rig's name is also the prefix of its bead ids.
@item agent
A worker that takes work from a rig's pool.  gascity renders a session
row joined with the agent's live status; a stopped pool slot has no
session yet.
@item session
The live, running instance of an agent --- the thing @kbd{s}, @kbd{w}
and @kbd{K} act on.  Every session belongs to an agent.
@item polecat
gascity's detail view of one agent (the @dfn{polecat} row): its work,
current run, transcript, mail and history (@pxref{Agent Detail}).
@item bead
An issue in a rig's store.  Bead display is delegated to beads.el;
gascity scopes the store by the bead id's rig prefix
(@pxref{Introduction}).
@item convoy
A collection of beads moved together through a workflow
(@pxref{Convoys}).
@item order
A scheduled or triggered unit of work that runs a command at a time or
interval (@pxref{Orders}).
@item sling
The one menu that routes a bead, a formula or free text to an agent
(@pxref{Sling and Dispatch}).
@item formula
A workflow template that expands into beads and runs
(@pxref{Dispatch a Formula}).
@item run
One instantiation of a formula, with a step ladder and a state
(@pxref{Runs and Live Events}).
@item step
One node of a run's ladder; the steps carry the run's progress
(@pxref{Run Detail}).
@item store
The per-city payload cache every view reads through: one cached
response per @command{gc} command line, shared by all views and kept
fresh for a short TTL (@pxref{Introduction}).
@item view
A read-only gascity buffer --- the cockpit, a dashboard, a list or a
detail buffer.  The full set is in @ref{View and Key Reference}.
@end table

