@node Installation
@chapter Installation and Requirements
@cindex installation


@menu
* Requirements::  Emacs, gc, beads.el and vui.
* Loading from a checkout::  Put lisp/ on the load-path.
* Building and installing with autotools::  autogen.sh, configure, make.
@end menu

@node Requirements
@section Requirements

@cindex requirements
@cindex dependencies
@table @asis
@item GNU Emacs 29.1 or later
The porcelain uses facilities (e.g.@: @code{tabulated-list} truncation,
modern @code{transient}) that assume a recent Emacs.
@item The @command{gc} CLI on @code{exec-path}
gascity shells out to @command{gc} for every read and every action.  A
bare command name is looked up on @code{exec-path}; set
@code{gascity-executable} to use an absolute path (@pxref{Customization and Theming}).
@item @code{beads.el}, @code{vui} and @code{transient} on the @code{load-path}
@code{beads.el} provides the @code{beads-meta}, @code{beads-section},
@code{beads-terminal} and @code{beads-pager} features that gascity builds
on; @code{vui} is the dashboard reconciler, and @code{transient} (0.10.1
or later) is the menu backend, which the Emacs 29.1--30 builds do not
bundle.
@item A running city (for live data)
With no reachable @command{gc}, a view never signals: each section whose
read failed shows one @samp{■ gc @dots{}: @var{reason}   g retry} line
and the others keep working.
@end table

@cindex vterm
@cindex eat
Optionally, install @code{vterm} or @code{eat} for a nicer terminal when
attaching to an agent's tmux session; without either, gascity falls back
to the built-in @code{term} (@pxref{Customization and Theming}).

The package header declares the full dependency set:

@example
(emacs "29.1") (transient "0.10.1") (vui "1.0.0")
(beads "0.1.0")
@end example

@noindent
where @code{beads} is beads.el, @code{vui} is its dashboard reconciler and
@code{transient} (0.10.1 or later) is the menu backend.  Emacs 31 and
later bundle a new enough @code{transient}; on 29.1--30 it comes from GNU
ELPA (@command{scripts/ci-deps} installs it in CI).

@node Loading from a checkout
@section Loading from a checkout

@cindex loading
Put gascity's @file{lisp} directory and its dependencies
(@pxref{Requirements}) on your @code{load-path}, then require the entry
point, which loads every module:

@lisp
(add-to-list 'load-path "/path/to/gascity.el/lisp")
(add-to-list 'load-path "/path/to/beads.el/lisp")
;; The vui bundled with the beads.el checkout, or a standalone copy.
(add-to-list 'load-path "/path/to/vui")
(require 'gascity)
@end lisp

@noindent
@code{beads.el} and @code{vui} are not on ELPA, so a fresh
@code{emacs -Q} must be told where they are: point the second entry at
the beads.el checkout and the third at the @code{vui} that checkout
bundles (for example
@file{beads.el/.eldev/31.1/packages/vui-1.4.0/}) or at a standalone
@code{vui} checkout.  @code{transient} (0.10.1 or later) is bundled
with Emacs 31 and later; on Emacs 29.1--30 install it from GNU ELPA.

@noindent
You are ready: run @kbd{M-x gascity-dashboard} (@pxref{Getting Started}).

@node Building and installing with autotools
@section Building and installing with autotools

@cindex autotools
@cindex autogen.sh
@cindex configure
@cindex make
@cindex make check
@cindex make install
@cindex Guix
gascity.el is a GNU-style autotools project.  From a checkout, build and
install it with:

@example
./autogen.sh
./configure --with-beads-dir="$HOME/workspace/beads.el"
make
make check
make install
@end example

@noindent
@command{autogen.sh} runs @command{autoreconf}.  @command{configure}
finds Emacs, byte-compiles every @file{lisp/*.el} with warnings promoted
to errors, and can be pointed at the non-ELPA dependencies
(@code{beads.el} and @code{vui}) and, on Emacs 29.1--30, at
@code{transient}:

@table @option
@item --with-beads-dir=@var{dir}
The beads.el checkout to build against (default
@file{$HOME/workspace/beads.el}).
@item --with-vui-dir=@var{dir}
The @code{vui} checkout to build against.  The default is the @code{vui}
bundled with @code{beads.el}, which deliberately wins over any
@code{emacs-vui} package from an ELPA or a distribution.
@item --with-transient-dir=@var{dir}
A directory containing @code{transient.el} to prepend to
@code{EMACSLOADPATH}, shadowing the older @code{transient} bundled with
Emacs 29.1--30.  The default is the ambient @code{EMACSLOADPATH} (and,
on Emacs 31+, the bundled copy).
@end table

@noindent
@command{make check} runs the ERT suite; it needs a live @command{gc} and
a city, so a checkout without one skips the few tests that require them.
@command{make install} installs the byte-compiled Lisp, the
@file{gascity-autoloads.el} and the Info manual.

@cindex guix shell
@cindex guix build
On Guix, @file{guix.scm} packages the same tree through
@code{gnu-build-system} and provides the development environment:

@example
guix shell -D -f guix.scm
./autogen.sh
./configure --with-beads-dir="$HOME/workspace/beads.el"
make && make check
@end example

@noindent
@command{guix build -f guix.scm} builds and installs the package the same
way.  Because @code{beads.el} and @code{vui} are not packaged for Guix,
@file{guix.scm} copies the sibling @file{beads.el} checkout into the store
when it is evaluated and passes its path as @code{--with-beads-dir} (the
@code{vui} it bundles becomes @code{--with-vui-dir}).  The checkout must
therefore exist before @command{guix build} or @command{guix shell} runs;
set @env{GASCITY_BEADS_DIR} to point elsewhere, or pin the dependency with
@code{git-fetch} for a build that does not rely on a sibling directory.

@noindent
@file{README.md} keeps a short install section; this manual is the full
reference.  The manual's own build targets are in @ref{Contributing},
and the lint and documentation-drift gates in
@ref{Linting and documentation drift}.

