@node Install and Start
@section Install and Start

gascity.el is an Emacs package that shells out to the @command{gc}
CLI.  Three steps get you to the cockpit:

@enumerate
@item
Load it.  Put the checkout's @file{lisp} directory and its dependencies
on the @code{load-path} and @code{(require 'gascity)}, or install the
package (@pxref{Installation}).
@item
Make sure @command{gc} is on @code{PATH} and the city is running.  No
reachable @command{gc} is not fatal: each failed section shows one
retry line and the others keep working (@pxref{Requirements}).
@item
Open the cockpit.  @code{gascity-dashboard} resolves the city by
walking up from @code{default-directory} for @file{city.toml}, so run
it from inside the city tree.  @kbd{M-x gascity} raises the dispatcher
transient instead, whose @strong{City} column starts and stops the city
(@pxref{The Cockpit}, @pxref{Actions}, @pxref{Customization and
Theming}).
@end enumerate

Inside any gascity buffer one set of keys means the same thing:
@key{TAB}/@kbd{S-@key{TAB}} move between things, @key{SPC} toggles the
thing at point, @key{RET} acts on it, @kbd{g} reloads, @kbd{q} buries,
@kbd{j} jumps to another view, @kbd{/} filters and @kbd{?} lists every
verb under its view key.  @xref{Buffers and Navigation}.

@c ====================================================================
@node Buffers and Navigation
@chapter Buffers and Navigation
@cindex navigation
@cindex section model

Every gascity buffer is read-only and keyboard-driven, and one set of
keys means the same thing in all of them: the vui views (cockpit,
detail views, Health) and the tabulated lists alike.  This chapter
documents those keys once; each later chapter adds only the keys unique
to its view.

@menu
* Moving and toggling::   TAB, S-TAB, SPC, RET, N, P and friends.
* The jump prefix::       @kbd{j}: go to another view.
* The ? dispatch::        Every verb under its view key.
* Filter menus::          @kbd{/} and its letters.
* Visual language::       Glyphs, times and section states.
* Objects at point::      What an action acts on.
* Lists::                 Pagination, sorting, the detail window.
@end menu

@node Moving and toggling
@section Moving and toggling

@cindex sections
@cindex things
@cindex collapsing
@cindex drawer
The vui views are built from @dfn{sections}: a header line followed by
its rows.  A @dfn{thing} is every line that carries something you can
act on: a section header, a row whose object is an agent, session,
bead, run, rig or event, a fold row (@samp{▸ stopped @dots{}}, a pool,
@samp{▸ 88 checks ok}), and a @samp{@dots{} N more} line.  The
summary lines at the top, blank lines and dim status lines are
decoration and are skipped.

@table @kbd
@item n
@kindex n
@fnindex next-line
Move down one line.
@item p
@kindex p
@fnindex previous-line
Move up one line.
@item N
@kindex N
@fnindex gascity-section-next
Jump to the next section header (the coarse counterpart to @kbd{n}).
@item P
@kindex P
@fnindex gascity-section-previous
Jump to the previous section header.
@item @key{TAB}
@itemx S-@key{TAB}
@kindex TAB
@kindex S-TAB
@fnindex gascity-thing-forward
@fnindex gascity-thing-backward
Move to the next (previous) thing.  At the last thing the motion wraps
to the first and echoes @samp{Wrapped}, as @code{forward-button} does.
@kbd{<tab>}, @kbd{<backtab>} and @kbd{S-<tab>} are bound too, so the
keys work in GUI frames and terminals alike.
@item @key{SPC}
@kindex SPC
@fnindex gascity-thing-toggle
Toggle the thing at point: on a section header, fold or unfold the
section; on a fold row, expand or collapse it in place; on any other
row, open or close its inline @dfn{drawer} --- a few dim @samp{│} lines
of detail read from data already loaded (no @command{gc} call).  On a
line with nothing to toggle it says so.  Folds and drawers are view
state: they survive a refresh.
@item @key{RET}
@kindex RET
Act on the thing at point --- the precise meaning depends on the view
(attach an agent's terminal, open a bead, open a run).  On a section
header it opens the section's full view.  @key{RET} never folds.
@item q
@kindex q
@fnindex quit-window
Bury the buffer.
@item g
@kindex g
Reload the view from @command{gc}, preserving point, folds and drawers.
@item ?
@kindex ?
The dispatch menu (@pxref{The ? dispatch}).
@item j
@kindex j
The jump prefix (@pxref{The jump prefix}).
@item /
@kindex /
The view's filter menu (@pxref{Filter menus}).
@item +
@itemx -
@kindex +
@kindex -
@fnindex gascity-section-more
@fnindex gascity-section-less
@vindex gascity-dashboard-section-batch
Show more (fewer) rows of the capped section at point, resolved from
its header, any of its rows or its @samp{@dots{} N more} line:
@code{gascity-dashboard-section-batch} rows (ten) at a time, never
fewer than the cap.  On a section with no hidden rows, @kbd{+} echoes
@samp{No section with more rows here}.  This works in the cockpit's sections, an unfolded
churn row, and the rig dashboard's bead sections; in the Runs view
@kbd{+}/@kbd{-} page the history.  The rows are already loaded, so no
@command{gc} call runs.  The expansion is view state: it survives
@kbd{g}, and @kbd{C-u g} resets it.
@end table

@noindent
@kbd{DEL} and @kbd{S-@key{SPC}} are deliberately unbound, since
@key{SPC} no longer scrolls; @kbd{C-v} and @kbd{M-v} still do, and the
views are short by design.

@cindex nudge, mnemonic
@cindex peek, mnemonic
@quotation Note
Because @kbd{N} and @kbd{P} take the section-motion keys and @kbd{p}
takes previous-line, the two actions that once lived there moved: agent
@dfn{nudge} is now @kbd{M} (``message'') and @dfn{peek} is now @kbd{v}.
@end quotation

@node The jump prefix
@section The jump prefix @kbd{j}

@cindex jump prefix
@kindex j
@fnindex gascity-jump-cockpit
@fnindex gascity-jump-agents
@fnindex gascity-jump-beads
@fnindex gascity-jump-health
@fnindex gascity-jump-cities
@fnindex gascity-jump-costs
@fnindex gascity-jump-rig
Views are reached through @kbd{j} followed by one letter, in every
gascity view.  (Single capitals are taken: @kbd{R}, for one, is
reset.)

@multitable @columnfractions .2 .8
@headitem Keys @tab View
@item @kbd{j j} @tab the cockpit (@pxref{The Cockpit})
@item @kbd{j a} @tab agents (@pxref{Agents})
@item @kbd{j r} @tab runs (@pxref{Runs and Live Events})
@item @kbd{j b} @tab beads in beads.el, scoped to the rig at point, else chosen: a rig or the city
@item @kbd{j m} @tab the mail inbox (@pxref{Mail})
@item @kbd{j e} @tab events (@pxref{Events})
@item @kbd{j h} @tab Health (@pxref{Health Costs and the Lighter})
@item @kbd{j c} @tab Cities (@pxref{Cities and Remote Cities})
@item @kbd{j o} @kbd{j v} @kbd{j d} @tab the order, convoy and Dolt lists (@pxref{Tabulated Lists})
@item @kbd{j g} @tab the dashboard of the rig at point, else chosen
@item @kbd{j $} @tab @command{gc costs} output (@pxref{Costs})
@end multitable

@noindent
The rig prompts of @kbd{j g} and @kbd{j b} complete over the rigs
gascity already knows and refresh that list in the background; they
never wait on @command{gc}.  A jump to a view that is not built yet
echoes so instead of failing.

@node The ? dispatch
@section The @kbd{?} dispatch

@cindex dispatch transient
@kindex ?
@fnindex gascity-dispatch
@kbd{?} opens @code{gascity-dispatch}, a transient menu of every verb
and view.  Each suffix sits under the key it has in the views, so the
menu teaches the view keys:

@table @asis
@item Jump
@kbd{j j} @dots{} @kbd{j $}, as above.
@item Agent at point
@kbd{M} nudge, @kbd{s} suspend, @kbd{w} wake, @kbd{K} kill, @kbd{D}
drain, @kbd{R} reset, @kbd{U} undrain, @kbd{t} attach.
@item Work
@kbd{S} sling, @kbd{c} bead actions, @kbd{m} mail actions.
@item City
@kbd{L} reload, @kbd{C} city lifecycle (start, stop, suspend), @kbd{O}
run an order, @kbd{W} toggle live refresh, @kbd{g} refresh, @kbd{/}
filter.
@end table

@noindent
Its heading names the city and its path.

@shot{dispatch-dark, The ? dispatch over the cockpit (ef-deuteranopia-dark)}

@node Filter menus
@section Filter menus

@cindex filter
@kindex /
@kbd{/} opens the view's filter menu.  Every change applies at once
(there is no ``apply'' step), @kbd{x} resets every filter, and one
letter means one thing in every menu:

@multitable @columnfractions .12 .48 .40
@headitem Key @tab Meaning @tab Views
@item @kbd{-w} @kbd{-n} @kbd{-o} @kbd{-m} @tab show wisps / nudge beads / order churn / message beads @tab cockpit
@item @kbd{-c} @tab unfold churn @tab cockpit, Events
@item @kbd{-r} @tab rig@dots{} @tab cockpit, Agents, Runs, sessions
@item @kbd{-W} @tab time window@dots{} @tab cockpit, Runs, Events, Mail
@item @kbd{-s} @tab state@dots{} @tab Agents, Runs, sessions, rigs, convoys
@item @kbd{-q} @tab search@dots{} @tab Agents, Events, Mail
@item @kbd{-t} @tab event type@dots{} @tab Events
@item @kbd{-l} @tab signal level@dots{} @tab Events
@item @kbd{-a} @tab actor / sender@dots{} @tab Events, Mail
@item @kbd{-p} @tab provider@dots{} @tab Agents
@item @kbd{-F} @tab formula@dots{} @tab Runs
@item @kbd{-u} @tab unread only @tab Mail
@item @kbd{-e} @kbd{-t} @tab enabled only / type@dots{} @tab orders
@item @kbd{-S} @tab sort by@dots{} (across all pages) @tab every list
@item @kbd{x} @tab reset all @tab every menu
@end multitable


@node Visual language
@section Visual language

@cindex glyphs
Every view uses the same glyphs, aligned with the Gas City web
dashboard:

@multitable @columnfractions .1 .9
@headitem Glyph @tab Meaning
@item @samp{●} @tab ok, running, active
@item @samp{○} @tab stopped or idle (not a problem)
@item @samp{▲} @tab watch (a warning)
@item @samp{■} @tab attention: stuck, failed, down
@item @samp{◐} @tab partial or stale data; the reason is in the tooltip
@item @samp{⬣} @tab run step active
@item @samp{◆} @tab run step done
@item @samp{·} @tab run step pending
@item @samp{✕} @tab run step failed
@item @samp{▸} @samp{▾} @tab a fold row, collapsed / expanded
@item @samp{@dots{}} @tab loading, or an action in flight on this row
@end multitable

@cindex relative times
Times are relative (@samp{3m}, @samp{2h}, @samp{yesterday},
@samp{Sep 22}) with the ISO timestamp as a tooltip.

@cindex section states
Every section shows its load the same way:

@table @asis
@item loading, no data yet
@samp{@dots{}} in the header.
@item read failed, no data
One line, @samp{■ gc status: @var{first line of the error}   g retry}.
@item refresh failed over good data
The rows stay; the header gets @samp{◐ stale}, or @samp{◐ timed out}
when the read hit its deadline, with the reason as a tooltip.
@item empty
@samp{none} in the header.
@end table

@noindent
A host that cannot be reached at all is shown once, as @samp{○ offline
@@host} in the view's header, not as an error in every section
(@pxref{Remote Cities}).  Views say what they hide --- @samp{(98 wisps
hidden)} --- and never print a line apologizing for data @command{gc}
does not provide.

@node Objects at point
@section Objects at point

@cindex object at point
Actions resolve the @dfn{object at point} through one precedence ladder:
an agent, then a bead id, then the current list row, then the buffer's
subject (the agent a detail view is @emph{about}).  This is why an action
key works whether point is on a specific row or anywhere in a detail view
that has a single subject.

@node Lists
@section Lists: pagination, sorting, detail

@cindex pagination
@cindex sorting
The tabulated lists size each page to the window and carry these keys in
addition to the standard @code{tabulated-list-mode} bindings (column
sorting on the header line, and so on):

@table @kbd
@item ]
@kindex ]
@fnindex gascity-tabulated-next-page
Next page.
@item [
@kindex [
@fnindex gascity-tabulated-prev-page
Previous page.
@item G
@kindex G
@fnindex gascity-tabulated-goto-page
Jump to a page number (prompts).
@item S
@kindex S
Sling (the same in every view); sort with a header click or @kbd{/ -S}
instead, which sorts across @emph{all} pages.
@item @key{SPC}
@kindex SPC @r{(lists)}
@fnindex gascity-tabulated-detail-toggle
Show the row at point in a @file{*gascity-detail*} side window, or close
it.  @kbd{C-o} shows it without selecting it and @kbd{C-c C-f} makes it
follow point; @kbd{q} closes it before burying the list.
@item /
@kindex /
Open the list's filter menu: changes apply at once, @kbd{x} resets,
@kbd{-S} sorts.
@end table

@noindent
The mode line shows @samp{Name [page/total] (filter)}; an over-long cell
is truncated to its column with an ellipsis and a @code{help-echo}
tooltip carrying the full value.

@c ====================================================================
@node The Cockpit
@chapter The Cockpit
@cindex cockpit
@fnindex gascity-dashboard

@kbd{M-x gascity-dashboard} opens the city's cockpit in
@code{gascity-dashboard-mode}: one short triage buffer answering, top to
bottom, what needs you, what is moving, who is working, what is queued
and what just happened.  A @dfn{city} is the workspace the cockpit
triages; @ref{Terminology} fixes the term.  No section shows more than
@code{gascity-dashboard-section-rows} rows (five); the rest is a
@samp{@dots{} N more} line whose @key{RET} opens the full view, and
@kbd{+}/@kbd{-} show more or fewer rows in place.

@shot{cockpit-dark, The cockpit of emacs-city (ef-deuteranopia-dark)}

@section What it shows

The header line names the city (with @samp{@@host} for a remote one),
the state of its live event stream (@pxref{Live Refresh}) and how long
ago it last refreshed.  The
buffer opens with the city and its path, then one summary line: agents
running out of total, live sessions, active and failed runs, ready
beads, unread mail and the beads store's size (@samp{◐} when
@command{gc} reports partial errors, with the reason as a tooltip).

@table @asis
@item Needs you
Stalled agents (running without a live session), sessions that crashed
or timed out and were not woken since, runs with no step progress for
@code{gascity-dashboard-run-idle-threshold} seconds, runs that failed,
beads reopened after their assignee died, beads labelled
@samp{gc:escalation} or @samp{hold:*}, unread mail and store-health
warnings --- @samp{■} before @samp{▲}.
@item Moving
Active runs with their step ladder (@samp{◆} done, @samp{⬣} active,
@samp{·} pending, @samp{✕} failed) and their live workers; in-progress
work outside a run is listed flat.  A drain step (one that fans out
into member runs) is active while one of its members is in progress,
and each member run nests under the run it drains for, with its own
workers under it:

@example
Moving  2 runs · 2 sub-runs · 2 workers
  ⬣ bs-f0ay   build-basic  ◆◆◆◆◆⬣····  implement      5/10   1h
    └ ⬣ bs-rj3o  do-work  ◆⬣·  implement  1/3   18m
        └ ● implementation-worker-1  bs-8qj7  Implement owned work  14s
@end example

@noindent
The header counts the top-level runs, then the sub-runs and workers;
the row cap, @kbd{+}/@kbd{-} and @samp{@dots{} N more} count top-level
runs.  A member whose parent is not active stays at the top level.  An
in-progress bead with no assignee reads @samp{unassigned} and counts as
no worker.
@item Agents
Running agents by recent activity, then idle ones; stopped agents fold
into one @samp{▸ stopped} line.  Named sessions such as the mayor are
agents too.
@item Work
Ready beads by priority, then age.  Wisps, nudge beads, order churn,
message beads and session beads are hidden, always with a
@samp{(N hidden)} count.
@item Activity
Recent events (@code{gascity-dashboard-window}, two hours by default).
Order firings, noise-bead lifecycle and bead updates fold into
@samp{×N} rows per 15 minutes; signal events never fold.
@item Rigs
One row per rig: prefix, path, agents running, work in progress.  The
city's HQ rig is listed too, so the count matches @kbd{M-x
gascity-rig-list} instead of silently omitting it.
@end table

Sections show their load state the common way (@pxref{Visual
language}).  An agent row with an action in flight shows @samp{@dots{}}
in place of its glyph until @command{gc} answers.

@cindex Needs you totals
Every time the cockpit renders with a status payload in hand it
publishes its Needs you @samp{■}/@samp{▲} totals and active-run count
for the session; the mode-line lighter (@pxref{The Mode-Line Lighter})
and the Cities view (@pxref{Cities and Remote Cities}) show them from there, without a
@command{gc} call of their own.

@shot{cockpit-light, The same cockpit in a light theme (ef-cyprus)}

@section Keys

Besides the shared keys (@pxref{Buffers and Navigation}):

@table @kbd
@item /
@kindex / @r{(cockpit)}
@fnindex gascity-dashboard-filter
The filter: @kbd{-w}, @kbd{-n}, @kbd{-o}, @kbd{-m} show wisps, nudge
beads, order churn and message beads; @kbd{-r} narrows to a rig;
@kbd{-W} sets the Activity window; @kbd{-c} unfolds churn.  Filters are
remembered per city for the session.
@item W
@kindex W @r{(cockpit)}
@fnindex gascity-dashboard-toggle-live
Toggle the city's live event stream (@pxref{Live Refresh}).  While it
runs, the cockpit refreshes when @code{gc events --follow} reports a
change; the header shows its state.
@item @key{RET}
@kindex RET @r{(cockpit)}
@fnindex gascity-dashboard-activate
On a section header, open the section's view; on an agent, attach its
terminal; on a run, open its detail; on a bead, open it in beads.el; on
a rig, open its dashboard.
@item i
@itemx v
@itemx d
@itemx t
Agent detail, peek, Dired and tmux on an agent row.
@item M
@itemx s
@itemx K
@itemx w
@itemx D
@itemx R
@itemx U
Nudge, suspend, kill, wake, drain, reset and undrain the agent at point;
on a rig row @kbd{s}, @kbd{r} and @kbd{R} suspend, resume and restart
the rig.
@item l
@kindex l @r{(cockpit)}
@fnindex gascity-dashboard-rig-log
The git log of the rig at point.
@item S
@itemx c
@itemx m
Sling, bead actions and mail actions.
@item L
@itemx C
@itemx O
Reload the city's configuration, the city lifecycle menu (start, stop,
suspend) and run an order.
@end table

@menu
* Watch the Cockpit::  Read city triage at a glance.
@end menu

@node Watch the Cockpit
@section Watch the Cockpit

@kbd{M-x gascity-dashboard} opens the city's cockpit, one short triage
buffer whose six sections answer, top to bottom, what needs you, what is
moving, who is working, what is queued and what just happened:
@strong{Needs you}, @strong{Moving}, @strong{Agents}, @strong{Work},
@strong{Activity} and @strong{Rigs}.  @xref{The Cockpit}.

The shared navigation keys carry you through it; @key{RET} opens the
view behind a section header, an agent, a run, a bead or a rig;
@kbd{+}/@kbd{-} show more or fewer rows of a capped section; @kbd{/}
opens the filter; @kbd{W} toggles the city's live event stream; @kbd{S},
@kbd{c} and @kbd{m} sling, act on a bead or act on mail; and @kbd{C} is
the city lifecycle menu, @kbd{O} runs an order.

If you want the counts in every mode line, turn on the global, opt-in
lighter (it never runs @command{gc} of its own):

@lisp
(gascity-mode-line-mode 1)
@end lisp

@noindent
@xref{The Mode-Line Lighter}.  With live refresh on, the cockpit
re-renders when an event arrives (@pxref{Live Refresh}).

@c ====================================================================
@node Agents
@chapter Agents
@cindex agents

An @dfn{agent} is a worker in a rig's pool and a @dfn{session} is its
running instance; a @dfn{polecat} is gascity's detail row for one agent
(@pxref{Terminology}).

@menu
* The Agents view::  Every agent of the city.
* Agent Detail::  One agent in detail.
* Inspect Agents and Sessions::  Find one agent and act on it.
* Attach to a Terminal::  Drive an agent's tmux session from Emacs.
@end menu

@node The Agents view
@section The Agents view

@fnindex gascity-agents
@kindex j a
@kbd{j a} (or @kbd{M-x gascity-agents}) lists every agent of the city in
@file{*gascity-agents:@: CITY*}: the configured agents from
@code{gc status} joined to their live sessions, plus named sessions
such as the mayor.  Each row shows the agent's state, last activity, the
bead on its hook and its provider.  Stalled agents (@samp{■}: running
by @command{gc}'s account, with no live session) are pinned to the top.

@shot{agents-dark, The Agents view (ef-deuteranopia-dark)}

@table @kbd
@item T
@kindex T @r{(agents)}
@fnindex gascity-agents-tree
Switch to the tree, @file{*gascity-agents-tree:@: CITY*}: city, then
rigs, then pools (with their @samp{scaled 0--2} bounds), then agents.
The @strong{City} and @strong{Named sessions} headers fold like a rig or
pool with @key{SPC}, showing @samp{▸}/@samp{▾}, and the fold survives
@kbd{g}.  @kbd{T} there switches back.
@item /
@kindex / @r{(agents)}
@fnindex gascity-agents-filter
Filter by state (@kbd{-s}; running by default, stalled agents are always
shown), rig (@kbd{-r}), provider (@kbd{-p}) and a search string
(@kbd{-q}).
@item @key{RET}
@itemx t
Attach the agent's terminal.
@item i
@itemx v
@itemx d
Agent detail, peek, Dired.
@item M
@itemx s
@itemx K
@itemx w
@itemx D
@itemx R
@itemx U
Nudge, suspend, kill, wake, drain, reset, undrain (@pxref{Actions}).
@end table

@shot{agents-tree-dark, The Agents tree: city rigs pools agents (ef-deuteranopia-dark)}

@noindent
The list shares the keys of every tabulated list (@pxref{Lists}); the
tree is a vui view with the section keys.

@node Agent Detail
@section Agent Detail
@cindex agent detail
@fnindex gascity-polecat-detail-at-point

@kbd{i} on an agent anywhere opens @file{*gascity-agent:@: NAME*}, the
@dfn{polecat} row (@pxref{Terminology}):

@table @asis
@item The header
Glyph, name, state and last activity; the session id and tmux name,
pool template and provider, worktree, and when the session was created.
@item Work
Every bead the agent has in progress (@samp{⬣}, with its run), the one
gc records as the session's current bead first; then the beads assigned
to it but not started (@samp{·}).  gc assigns a run's later steps to its
worker up front, so those read @samp{not started}, never as the work at
hand.
@item Run
The current bead's run: its step ladder, active step and progress.
@item Transcript
The last ten entries of the agent's session log.
@item Mail
Your mail from or to this agent.
@item History
The agent's recently closed beads.
@end table

@cindex work_dir
@noindent
Beads are gathered by assignee (the runtime session name and the
qualified name) and by worktree (@code{metadata.work_dir}), so work a
finished agent's beads were reassigned away from is still shown.

@table @kbd
@item f
@kindex f @r{(agent detail)}
@fnindex gascity-session-follow-log
Follow the agent's log (@code{gc session logs -f}, raw text) in
@file{*gascity-log:@: TARGET*}; over TRAMP it runs as a local ssh pipe.
@item v
Peek at the agent's recent terminal output.
@item @key{RET}
@fnindex gascity-session-detail-activate
Open the bead at point in beads.el.
@item g
@fnindex gascity-polecat-detail-refresh
Reload, preserving point.
@item M @r{/} s @r{/} K @r{/} w @r{/} D @r{/} R @r{/} U @r{/} d @r{/} t
The agent keys; they act on the buffer's agent wherever point is.
@item c
@itemx S
Bead actions and sling.
@end table

@node Inspect Agents and Sessions
@section Inspect Agents and Sessions

@kbd{j a} lists every agent of the city, or @kbd{M-x gascity-agents};
@kbd{T} switches to the city/rigs/pools/agents tree.  Each row shows the
agent's state, last activity, current bead and provider, with stalled
agents pinned to the top.  @xref{The Agents view}.

@key{RET} (or @kbd{t}) attaches the agent's terminal; @kbd{i} opens its
detail view with its work, current run, transcript, mail and history;
@kbd{M} nudges, @kbd{s} suspends, @kbd{w} wakes, @kbd{K} kills,
@kbd{D} drains, @kbd{R} resets and @kbd{v} peeks at recent output.
@xref{Agent Detail}, @ref{Actions}.

The same agents appear in the @strong{Sessions} tabulated list, with
their rig, state, provider and working directory; @key{RET} and @kbd{t}
attach, @kbd{i} opens the detail, and @kbd{d} opens Dired in the
worktree.  @xref{Sessions}.

@node Attach to a Terminal
@section Attach to a Terminal

@kbd{t} on an agent --- in the cockpit, the Agents view, the session
list, the rig dashboard or the agent detail --- opens a terminal buffer
holding a live @command{tmux} client attached to the agent's session.
@xref{The Agents view}, @ref{Agent Detail}.

A tmux client draws on the alternate screen, so scrolling goes through
tmux: @kbd{C-b [} enters copy-mode and @key{PageUp}/@key{PageDown}
page through the history.  For Magit-flavoured reading, @kbd{C-c s}
toggles @code{gascity-terminal-scroll-mode}, which translates the Emacs
scroll keys into copy-mode sequences so the agent receives no keys.
@xref{Actions}.

