@end quotation

@menu
* Manage Rigs::  Suspend, resume and restart rigs.
@end menu

@node Manage Rigs
@section Manage Rigs

A rig is a repository that owns a beads store and runs its own pool of
agents.  The @strong{Rigs} tabulated list shows each rig's prefix,
status, branch and store; @key{RET} opens its dashboard, @kbd{b} opens
its beads in beads.el, @kbd{s}/@kbd{r}/@kbd{R} suspend, resume and
restart it (restart confirms, since it kills the rig's sessions), and
@kbd{d} opens Dired in the rig directory.  @xref{Rigs}.

@kbd{M-x gascity-rig-dashboard} (or @kbd{j g}) opens the single-rig
counterpart to the cockpit: header, agents, ready and in-progress beads,
orders and Dolt, each section loaded independently.  @kbd{b} opens the
whole rig's bead board, and the agent keys act on the rig's agents.
