@node Work Remotely
@section Work Remotely

Every view works the same on a city on another host.  Open any directory
of the city over TRAMP and start a view from there; every read, action
and refresh then runs @command{gc} on that host, never a silent local
fallback:

@example
C-x d /ssh:user@@example.com:/home/user/city/ @key{RET}
M-x gascity-dashboard
@end example

@noindent
Buffer names are host-qualified, so a local and a remote view of the
same city coexist; the header line shows @samp{@@host}.
@xref{Remote Cities}.

For a single-hop ssh-family host, background reads run as local
@code{ssh -T} pipes rather than TRAMP processes, with a per-host
scheduler, a deadline on every process and an @samp{○ offline} state
with backoff probes when a host cannot be reached; tmux attach spawns a
local @code{ssh -t HOST} in the terminal backend.  @xref{Transport},
