@node Runs and Live Events
@chapter Runs and Live Events
@cindex runs
@cindex workflow runs

A @dfn{run} is one instantiation of a formula, a workflow template that
expands into beads; its ladder is a series of @dfn{steps}
(@pxref{Terminology}).

@menu
* The Runs view::  Workflow run cards.
* Run Detail::  One run in detail.
* Live Refresh::  One event stream per city.
* Events::  The event log.
* Follow Runs and Live Events::  Follow a workflow run and the event log.
@end menu

@node The Runs view
@section The Runs view

@fnindex gascity-runs
@kindex j r
@kbd{j r} (or @kbd{M-x gascity-runs}) shows the city's workflow runs in
@file{*gascity-runs:@: CITY*}, as two-line cards grouped into Active,
Waiting and Failed:

@example
Runs  emacs-city   1 active · 0 waiting · 51 done · 11 failed

Active  1
  ⬣ be-52m5  build-basic                              beads.el   2h
     ◆⬣········  requirements   1/10   ● requirements-planner-1  be-bcb5

Failed  1 · last 24h
  ✕ be-bn2   build-basic                              beads.el   2h
     ◆◆◆◆◆◆◆✕◆◆  review         9/10   control_dispatch_error
@end example

@shot{runs-dark, The Runs view (ef-deuteranopia-dark)}

@noindent
A card's second line is the step ladder (@pxref{Visual language}), the
active step, progress, and the worker on it.  @command{gc} has no run
summary (@pxref{Capability Gaps}), so a run is derived from its bead
graph: the root bead of kind @code{workflow} and every bead that names
it as @code{gc.root_bead_id}, read from the city store and every rig
store.  The cockpit's Moving section uses the same ladder, so the two
always agree.  A drain member run's card nests under its parent's in
Active (@samp{└}, indented), and the section counts it as a sub-run.

The summary line counts every run all-time.  The Failed section is
windowed to @code{gascity-runs-failed-window} (24 hours by default) and
says so; a failure older than the window is not lost, it stays in the
Closed history, whose count is the summary's done plus failed.  So a
failed run is always in the Closed archive, even once the Failed window
has moved past it.

@table @kbd
@item @key{RET}
@fnindex gascity-runs-activate
Open the run's detail (@pxref{Run Detail}).
@item F
@fnindex gascity-runs-follow
Follow the run --- the persistent twin of the momentary @kbd{F}
follow offer a formula sling echoes on launch.
@item b
@fnindex gascity-runs-root-bead
Open the run's root bead in beads.el.
@item @key{SPC}
Open the card's drawer: the full step ladder, one line per step.
@item H
@fnindex gascity-runs-history
Show the Closed section: every closed run (done and failed), newest
first, @code{gascity-runs-history-page} (20) per page; @kbd{+}
(@code{gascity-runs-more}) shows the next page.
@item /
@fnindex gascity-runs-filter
Filter by rig (@kbd{-r}), formula (@kbd{-F}), state (@kbd{-s}: active,
failed, done) and window (@kbd{-W}; the Failed section defaults to
@code{gascity-runs-failed-window}, 24 hours).  Filters are remembered
per city.
@item i
@itemx v
@itemx t
Detail, peek and attach for the run's worker at point.
@end table

@node Run Detail
@section Run Detail

@fnindex gascity-run-show
@key{RET} on a run --- in the cockpit or the Runs view --- opens
@file{*gascity-run:@: ID*}:

@example
⬣ be-52m5  build-basic                       beads.el · started 2h
  formula  build-basic (graph.v2)   source ~/.gc/cache/@dots{}/build-basic.formula.toml
  plans    requirements.md · implementation-plan.md · review-report.md
  convoy   be-93dg  open 0/1  project-switch-scope

Steps  1/10                                    C show control nodes
  ◆ prepare                   be-5aht   pass     run-operator      2h
  ⬣ requirements              be-bcb5   iter 1   ● requirements-planner-1
  ▾ review                    be-mqhp   loop
      · setup-build-basic-review  be-bdcr
      ▸ build-basic-review-loop   be-zdon   loop
@end example

@noindent
The steps are the run's beads arranged by step: iterations hang under
their step, nested steps under theirs.  A step whose children are
plain iterations shows its latest one inline (@samp{iter N}); any other
step with children is a fold row, open while something beneath it is
active or failed.  Under a drain step, its member runs are listed
with their ladders (@samp{└ ⬣ bs-0c3f  do-work  ◆⬣·  implement 1/3});
@key{RET} on one opens that run's detail.  The @samp{plans} line lists
the run's plan files; @key{RET} on one visits it, on the city's host.

@table @kbd
@item @key{RET}
@fnindex gascity-run-activate
Open the bead, plan file or worker at point.
@item b
@fnindex gascity-run-root-bead
Open the root bead in beads.el.
@item C
@fnindex gascity-run-toggle-control
Show or hide control nodes (spec, scope check, finalize).
@item i
@itemx v
@itemx t
Detail, peek and attach for the worker at point.
@item g
@fnindex gascity-run-refresh
Reload.
@end table

@noindent
Opening a run from the Runs view costs no @command{gc} call: both share
one read.

@node Live Refresh
@section Live Refresh
@cindex live refresh
@cindex event stream
@fnindex gascity-live-toggle
@kindex W

Views don't poll.  @dfn{Live refresh} keeps a view in step with its
city's @dfn{store} and event stream without a timer
(@pxref{Terminology}).  While at least one view of a city is open, the
city runs @emph{one} @code{gc events --follow} stream; events are collected
for @code{gascity-live-debounce} seconds (2.5) and then only the
sections they affect re-read: a session or agent event refreshes the
agent sections, a bead event the work and run sections, a mail event
the mail counts, and so on.  The last view of a city to close stops its
stream.

The header line shows the stream's state:

@table @samp
@item ● live
The stream is running.
@item ○ live off
You turned it off with @kbd{W}; @kbd{g} still refreshes.
@item ○ live: reconnecting (@var{N}s)
The stream dropped; it reconnects after 2, 5, 15, then every 60 seconds
(@code{gascity-live-backoff}), resuming after the last event it saw, so
nothing is missed, and then refreshes everything once.  @kbd{g}
reconnects at once.
@item ○ live: supervisor down
@command{gc} serves events from the supervisor.  With it down the
stream and the event reads fail, while every other section keeps
working; @kbd{g} still refreshes.
@item ○ offline @@host
The host cannot be reached (@pxref{Remote Cities}).
@end table

@noindent
The stream's error output goes to @file{*gascity-live:@: CITY*}; its
last line is the reason shown in the header.

@kbd{W} (@code{gascity-live-toggle}) turns the stream off or on for the
city; @code{gascity-live-enabled} sets the default.  A remote city's
stream runs as a local @code{ssh -T} pipe, never on a TRAMP channel.
For remote methods plain ssh cannot reach (docker, sudo, multi-hop),
gascity polls @code{gc events} every @code{gascity-live-poll-interval}
seconds (30) instead.

@node Events
@section Events
@cindex events
@fnindex gascity-events
@kindex j e

@kbd{j e} (or @kbd{M-x gascity-events}) lists the city's
@code{gc events} for a time window in
@file{*gascity-events:@: CITY*}, newest first.  Churn --- order
firings and noise-bead lifecycles --- folds into one @samp{▸ @dots{} ×N}
row per 15 minutes; signal events (@code{gascity-dashboard-event-levels})
never fold and carry their @samp{■}/@samp{▲} in the Sig column.  With
live refresh on, new events are appended as they arrive.

@shot{events-dark, The Events view (ef-deuteranopia-dark)}

@table @kbd
@item @key{RET}
@fnindex gascity-events-visit
Drill in: a bead subject opens in beads.el, a session subject opens the
agent's detail, a @samp{×N} row narrows the view to that churn group,
any other event shows its fields.
@item b
@itemx i
Open the event's bead, or its agent's detail.
@item /
Filter by window (@kbd{-W}), type (@kbd{-t}), actor (@kbd{-a}), signal
level (@kbd{-l}), search (@kbd{-q}); @kbd{-c} unfolds churn.
@item W
Toggle the city's live event stream.
@end table

@node Follow Runs and Live Events
@section Follow Runs and Live Events

@kbd{j r} shows the city's workflow runs as cards grouped into Active,
Waiting and Failed, each with its step ladder and workers, derived from
the run's bead graph.  @key{RET} opens the run's detail (its steps,
iterations, nested and drain-member runs, plan files and control nodes),
@kbd{F} follows a run (the launch offer's momentary @kbd{F} made
permanent), @kbd{H} pages the history, @kbd{b} opens the run's root bead
and @kbd{/} filters by rig, formula, state and window.  @xref{Runs and Live Events},
@xref{Run Detail}.

@kbd{j e} lists the city's events, newest first, folding routine churn
into @samp{×N} rows and never folding signal events; @key{RET} drills
into a bead, a session or a churn group.  @xref{Events}.

Nothing polls.  While a view of a city is open, one
@code{gc events --follow} stream per city refreshes only the sections
the events touch; @kbd{W} turns the stream off and on and the header
line shows its state (live, off, reconnecting, supervisor down,
offline).  @xref{Live Refresh}.

