@defvr {User Option} gascity-terminal-preload-idle
Obsolete alias of @code{beads-terminal-tmux-preload-idle}.
@end defvr

@vindex gascity-terminal-status-interval
@defvr {User Option} gascity-terminal-status-interval
Obsolete alias of @code{beads-terminal-tmux-status-interval}.
@end defvr

@subheading The cockpit

@vindex gascity-dashboard-section-rows
@defopt gascity-dashboard-section-rows
Maximum number of rows a cockpit section shows (default 5); the rest
collapse into a @samp{@dots{} N more} line that opens the full view.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-dashboard-section-batch
@defopt gascity-dashboard-section-batch
Rows @kbd{+} adds to (and @kbd{-} takes from) a capped section at point
(default 10).  The cockpit sections, the rig dashboard's bead sections
and an unfolded churn row start at their cap; @kbd{+} shows this many
more, @kbd{-} this many fewer, never below the cap.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-dashboard-churn-unfold-rows
@defopt gascity-dashboard-churn-unfold-rows
Most events @kbd{SPC} unfolds under a cockpit @samp{×N} churn row
(default 20); the rest is a @samp{@dots{} N more} line whose @kbd{RET}
opens the Events view narrowed to that churn group.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-dashboard-window
@defopt gascity-dashboard-window
The Activity section's time window, a @code{gc events --since} duration
(default @code{"2h"}); @kbd{/ -W} changes it per city.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-events-window
@defopt gascity-events-window
Default time window of the Events view, a @code{gc events --since}
duration (default @code{"2h"}); days are passed to @command{gc} as hours
(its durations have no @samp{d} unit).
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-dashboard-run-idle-threshold
@defopt gascity-dashboard-run-idle-threshold
Seconds without step progress after which an active run is listed in
Needs you (default 1800).
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-dashboard-agent-idle-threshold
@defopt gascity-dashboard-agent-idle-threshold
Seconds of inactivity after which a running agent counts as idle
(default 3600); only the Agents section's running/idle split reads it.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-event-levels
@defopt gascity-event-levels
Which event types are signals: an alist of (@var{regexp} . @var{level}),
@var{level} @code{attention} (@samp{■}) or @code{watch} (@samp{▲}); the
first match wins and a type no entry matches is a plain event.  Signal
events are never folded into churn.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-live-enabled
@defopt gascity-live-enabled
Whether views keep their city's event stream running (default
@code{t}); @kbd{W} flips it per city.  See @ref{Live Refresh}.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-live-debounce
@defopt gascity-live-debounce
Seconds events are collected before their views are invalidated
(default 2.5).  The first event of a batch arms the timer; later ones
join the batch, so a view is at most this late under a trickle.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-live-backoff
@defopt gascity-live-backoff
Seconds to wait before each reconnect attempt, the last element repeating
(default @code{(2 5 15 60)}); the sequence restarts once a stream stayed
up for @code{gascity-live-stable-after} seconds.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-live-stable-after
@defopt gascity-live-stable-after
Seconds a stream must stay up before its backoff resets (default 15).
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-live-confirm-after
@defopt gascity-live-confirm-after
Seconds a (re)started stream must stay up before it counts as live
(default 3).  @command{gc} prints nothing until an event arrives, so a
fresh @code{gc events --follow} cannot prove it connected; its first
event confirms it at once.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-live-poll-interval
@defopt gascity-live-poll-interval
Seconds between event polls for a city without a stream (default 30),
for remote methods a plain ssh cannot reach (docker, sudo, multi-hop).
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-live-poll-watch
@defopt gascity-live-poll-watch
How long each poll waits for a first event when none is pending
(default @code{"2s"}).  A poll is @code{gc events --watch --after SEQ
--timeout} this: @command{gc} replays every event after SEQ and exits at
once, or waits this long for one.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-live-poll-bootstrap
@defopt gascity-live-poll-bootstrap
The @code{gc events --since} window of a poll that knows no seq yet
(default @code{"60s"}); it must cover @code{gascity-live-poll-interval}.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-live-events-reconcile
@defopt gascity-live-events-reconcile
Seconds between re-reads of a city's event feed (default 600), to
reconcile events missed across a reconnect gap with @command{gc}.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-live-in-batch
@defopt gascity-live-in-batch
When non-@code{nil}, streams also start in a batch (noninteractive)
Emacs (default @code{nil}), so tests and batch scripts that open views
never spawn a long-lived @code{gc events --follow}.
@end defopt

@subheading Health, Cities and the lighter

@vindex gascity-health-doctor-timeout
@defopt gascity-health-doctor-timeout
Seconds before a @command{gc doctor} run is killed (default 300).
Doctor runs every check in sequence, so it gets a longer deadline than
@code{gascity-remote-async-timeout}.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-remote-hosts
@defopt gascity-remote-hosts
Remote hosts whose cities the Cities view lists, as TRAMP prefixes
(@code{"/ssh:build-box:"}) or bare host names (meaning
@code{"/ssh:@var{host}:"}).  Hosts visited this session are listed
without being named here.  Default @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-pulse-store-samples
@defopt gascity-pulse-store-samples
How many store-size samples to keep per city for Health's sparkline
(default 40).
@end defopt

@subheading Runs

@vindex gascity-runs-history-page
@defopt gascity-runs-history-page
Closed runs per history page of the Runs view (default 20).
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-runs-failed-window
@defopt gascity-runs-failed-window
How far back the Runs view's Failed section looks (default
@code{"24h"}); @kbd{/ -W} overrides it.
@end defopt

@subheading Sling and formulas

@vindex gascity-sling-var-readers
@defopt gascity-sling-var-readers
Alist of formula var names to the readers overriding the heuristic,
@code{(VAR-NAME . READER)} (default @code{nil}).  @var{reader} is a typed
reader, any function of one infix object, or an infix class symbol; an
unmatched var falls through to @code{gascity-sling-formula--var-class}.
@end defopt

@subheading The store and scheduling

@vindex gascity-store-ttl-alist
@defopt gascity-store-ttl-alist
Freshness per read kind, @code{(KIND . TTL)} (default @code{((status .
5) (bd . 15) (doctor . manual))}).  @var{ttl} is a number of seconds or
the symbol @code{manual} (fresh until invalidated); kinds not listed use
@code{gascity-store-default-ttl}.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-store-default-ttl
@defopt gascity-store-default-ttl
Freshness in seconds of a read kind absent from
@code{gascity-store-ttl-alist} (default 5).
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-store-offline-backoff
@defopt gascity-store-offline-backoff
Seconds between reconnect probes of an offline host (default @code{(2 5
15 60)}); the Nth retry waits the Nth element and the last repeats.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-store-action-followups
@defopt gascity-store-action-followups
Seconds after a completed action at which its kinds are invalidated again
(default @code{(5 15 45 90 180)}); @command{gc} does not report all the
transitions an action sets off, so the views re-read what it touched.
Only visible views actually re-read.  @code{nil} disables the follow-ups.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-store-background-kinds
@defopt gascity-store-background-kinds
Read kinds that yield to every other kind in a host's read queue
(default @code{(events bd convoy order)}): the heavy or high-churn ones
must not make a light read wait on a capped remote host.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-store-refetch-hidden
@defopt gascity-store-refetch-hidden
When non-@code{nil}, an invalidated entry is re-read even when no view of
it is visible (default @code{nil}): a buried view's entries are just
marked stale and re-read when the view is shown again, so a city's event
stream does not make hidden views spawn @command{gc}.
@end defopt

@vindex gascity-timer-watchdog-interval
@defopt gascity-timer-watchdog-interval
Seconds between runs of the watchdog that rescues lost deferred calls
(default 0.5): a deferred call whose own timer TRAMP's timer suspension
discarded runs at most this long after it was due.
@end defopt

@noindent
The remote options --- @code{gascity-remote-transport},
@code{gascity-remote-ssh-options}, @code{gascity-remote-max-inflight},
@code{gascity-remote-async-timeout}, @code{gascity-remote-sync-timeout}
--- are described in @ref{Remote Cities}.

@section Context overrides

@vindex gascity-context-city
@vindex gascity-context-rig
@fnindex gascity-context-clear-cache
gascity resolves the @dfn{current} city and rig from
@code{default-directory}.  Bind @code{gascity-context-city} to an absolute
path or @code{gascity-context-rig} to a rig name to override that
resolution, and run @kbd{M-x gascity-context-clear-cache} to forget cached
resolutions.

@section Faces

@cindex faces
The @code{gascity-faces} group defines the porcelain's state colors, each
inheriting from a standard face so it tracks your theme:

@table @code
@item gascity-header
Section headers (bold).
@item gascity-city
The city name (keyword face).
@item gascity-rig
A rig name (function-name face).
@item gascity-running
A running agent or service (success).
@item gascity-stopped
A stopped agent (shadow).
@item gascity-suspended
A suspended rig or agent (warning).
@item gascity-warning
A watch state, @samp{▲} (warning).
@item gascity-failed
A failed or errored state (error).
@item gascity-dim
Secondary, de-emphasized text (shadow).
@end table

@section Theming

@cindex themes
@cindex screenshots, theme
gascity does not impose a theme of its own: every face it defines
inherits from a standard face, so the porcelain follows whatever theme
you load.  The manual's screenshots standardize on a single dark theme,
@code{ef-deuteranopia-dark}, so the images match what most users see.
The one deliberate exception is @code{cockpit-light}, captured in
@code{ef-cyprus} beside its @code{cockpit-dark} twin to demonstrate the
same buffer under a light and a dark theme (@pxref{The Cockpit}); every
other image is a @code{-dark} capture of @code{ef-deuteranopia-dark}.

@c ====================================================================
@node Capability Gaps
@appendix Capability Gaps
@cindex capability gaps
@cindex missing data

gascity shows only what the @command{gc} CLI exposes; it never calls
the supervisor's HTTP API@.  The following are not available in gascity
because @command{gc} does not expose them.  Where a view would need
one, it leaves the item out rather than printing an apology.

@table @asis
@item Costs as data
@command{gc costs} has no @option{--json} and no per-run or daily
aggregates, so costs are shown as @command{gc}'s text (@pxref{Costs}),
annotated when runs recorded no usage, and the cockpit shows no usage.
@item Sessions awaiting input
There is no @code{gc session pending} listing and no way to answer an
approval prompt from the CLI, so Needs you cannot list agents waiting
for you and agent rows have no approve/deny keys.
@item Context use and model
@code{gc session list --json} carries no context-window percentage and
no model, so the agent views show neither.
@item Run summaries
There is no @code{gc runs --json}; runs, their phase and their step
ladder are derived from the beads of the run's graph.
@item Reading mail as another identity
@code{gc mail inbox} has no @option{--as}, so the inbox is always the
operator's.
@item Supervisor uptime
@code{gc status} reports the controller's pid but not how long it has
been up, so Health shows no uptime.
@item bd and dolt versions
@code{gc version} reports only @command{gc}; the @command{bd} and
@command{dolt} versions appear in Health only after a doctor run, whose
report is the one place that carries them.
@item Run counts per city
No single read reports a city's active runs, so the Cities view shows
them only for cities whose cockpit is open.
@end table

@c ====================================================================
@node Troubleshooting
@chapter Troubleshooting

@cindex troubleshooting
@cindex diagnostics
Every failure has a visible cause; nothing pops a modal error.  This
chapter maps the common symptoms to their cause and fix.

@menu
* A section shows a failed read::   One section blank or stale.
* gc is not found::                 The executable on PATH.
* No city here::                    Context from default-directory.
* Remote city is offline or slow::  ssh, TRAMP and the scheduler.
* Live refresh stopped::            The event stream and its backoff.
* The terminal does not open::      Backend, tmux and scroll.
* Beads open in the wrong store::   default-directory and rig prefixes.
* Where the errors go::             The log buffer and debug options.
@end menu

@node A section shows a failed read
@section A section shows a failed read

@cindex failed section
@cindex retry
A vui view renders each section from its own read, so a failed read
blanks only that section:

@example
■ gc status: exit 1   g retry
@end example

@noindent
Press @kbd{g} to retry the read; the other sections keep working.  A
read that times out keeps its last good data, marked @samp{◐ timed
out}; raise @code{gascity-remote-async-timeout} if @command{gc} is
legitimately slow (@pxref{Scheduling}).  A stale-looking view is
usually the store's short TTL, not a failure: @kbd{g} always re-reads.

@node gc is not found
@section @command{gc} is not found

@cindex gc not found
@cindex exec-path
If every section fails with @samp{gc: not found}, the CLI is not on
Emacs's @code{exec-path}.  Install it, add its directory to
@code{exec-path}, or set @code{gascity-executable} to an absolute path
(@pxref{Customization and Theming}).  On a remote host the same name is resolved by
probing the profile directories in @code{beads-remote-search-path}
(@pxref{Finding gc}).

@node No city here
@section No city here

@cindex city not found
gascity finds the city by walking up from @code{default-directory} for
a @file{city.toml}.  Open a view from inside the city tree, bind
@code{gascity-context-city} to its path, or clear a cached resolution
with @kbd{M-x gascity-context-clear-cache} (@pxref{Customization and Theming}).
A rig that lives outside the city tree is resolved by asking
@command{gc}, so rig scoping does not need the checkout under point.

@node Remote city is offline or slow
@section Remote city is offline or slow

@cindex offline host
@cindex TRAMP freeze
A host that cannot be reached flips the whole city to @samp{○ offline
@@host}; its queue pauses and one probe retries with backoff
(@pxref{Scheduling}).  If a remote city freezes Emacs inside a TRAMP
wait, see @ref{ssh configuration} for the two ssh settings
(@code{ForwardX11} and connection sharing) that cause it.  Reads and
actions already run over a local @code{ssh} pipe and never block Emacs;
only Dired, the first contact with a host and the @code{tramp} transport
use TRAMP (@pxref{Transport}).

@node Live refresh stopped
@section Live refresh stopped

@cindex live refresh, stopped
@cindex event stream
No view polls on a timer.  A city refreshes live only while a view of it
is attached and @code{gascity-live-enabled} is non-@code{nil}; @kbd{W}
flips that per city, and @kbd{g} reconnects the stream
(@pxref{Live Refresh}).  With the stream off, @kbd{g} is the refresh.  A
stalled stream resumes gap-free with the 2/5/15/60-second backoff.

@node The terminal does not open
@section The terminal does not open

@cindex terminal backend
Attaching needs a backend.  gascity auto-detects @code{vterm}, then
@code{eat}, then the built-in @code{term}; force one with
@code{gascity-terminal-backend} (@pxref{Customization and Theming}).  The @kbd{t}
key reaches tmux through a local @code{ssh -t} for a remote city, and
only for the ssh-family TRAMP methods (@pxref{Remote buffers}).  For
scrolling and copy-mode, see @ref{Actions}.

@node Beads open in the wrong store
@section Beads open in the wrong store

@cindex bead store, wrong
Beads.el picks its store from @code{default-directory}, so gascity
binds @code{default-directory} to the owning rig's repo path (from the
bead id prefix) before calling @code{beads-show} or
@code{beads-dashboard}.  If a delegated view lands on the wrong store,
the bead id's prefix did not match a rig; check @kbd{j b} from the rig
whose beads you meant.

@node Where the errors go
@section Where the errors go

@cindex gascity-log
@cindex debug logging
Actions never pop a modal error.  The echo area shows the first line of
@command{gc}'s error; the full error goes to the city's
@file{*gascity-log:@: CITY*} buffer (@file{*gascity-log:@:
CITY@@host*} remotely).  Turn on @code{gascity-enable-debug} and raise
@code{gascity-debug-level} to @code{verbose} to log every
@command{gc} invocation (@pxref{Customization and Theming}).

