@node Module layout
@section Module layout

@cindex modules
gascity.el is organized as a stack of small modules, lowest first:

@table @file
@item gascity-reader.el
The data plane: the one place that runs @command{gc} and decodes its
JSON, synchronously and asynchronously, locally, over TRAMP or over a
local ssh pipe.
@item gascity-store.el
The per-city payload store every view reads through: caching, in-flight
dedup, the per-host scheduler, deadlines, offline hosts and the
asynchronous action runner.
@item gascity-remote.el
Remote paths, host-qualified buffer names, and the ssh argv builders
for attach and the ssh pipe transport.
@item gascity-command.el
@itemx gascity-types.el
@itemx gascity-command-status.el
The EIEIO command layer (built on beads.el's @code{beads-meta}): typed
@command{gc} commands, argument construction, execution and parsing.
@item gascity-domain.el
The typed read-payload objects (rig, session, agent, convoy, mail, order)
decoded from @command{gc}'s JSON.
@item gascity-context.el
Resolves the current city and rig from @code{default-directory}.
@item gascity-section.el
The shared vui base mode and the section model.
@item gascity-ui.el
The shared visual language: glyphs, relative times, section states and
the filter-menu builders.
@item gascity-pulse.el
What open cockpits publish for the session (Needs you totals, run
counts, store-size samples) and the mode-line lighter.
@item gascity-dashboard.el
The city cockpit, the @kbd{?} dispatch and the @kbd{j} jump prefix.
@item gascity-live.el
The per-city @code{gc events --follow} stream and its routing.
@item gascity-agents.el
@itemx gascity-runs.el
The Agents view and tree; the Runs view.
@item gascity-health.el
@itemx gascity-cities.el
The Health view and @command{gc costs}; the Cities list.
@item gascity-status.el
The agent-tree joins (city, rigs, pools) shared by the rig dashboard.
@item gascity-rig.el
@itemx gascity-session.el
@itemx gascity-run.el
The rig dashboard and the agent and run detail views.
@item gascity-tabulated.el
The six tabulated lists, their pagination and their filter transients.
@item gascity-action.el
The mutating-command dispatch and its sub-transients.
@item gascity-terminal.el
Terminal-backend selection, tmux attach, and the mode-line status mirror.
@item gascity-custom.el
@itemx gascity-error.el
User options and faces; the error hierarchy.
@end table

@node Building this manual
@section Building this manual

@cindex makeinfo
@cindex Texinfo
The manual is a single Texinfo source, @file{doc/gascity.texi}, built by
the autotools @code{info_TEXINFOS} machinery (@pxref{Building and
installing with autotools}).  From the top level:

@example
make info       # gascity.info
make html       # styled multi-page HTML
make pdf        # gascity.pdf
@end example

@noindent
@command{make html} splits the manual into one page per node and inlines
@file{manual.css} into every page with @code{makeinfo --css-include};
it also copies @file{doc/images} beside the pages, so the output is
self-contained.  @file{doc/screenshots/README.md} documents how the
committed images are produced.

@node Linting and documentation drift
@section Linting and documentation drift

@cindex linting
@cindex package-lint
@cindex checkdoc
@cindex documentation drift
@cindex generated tables
Two gates keep the sources honest:

@table @asis
@item @command{make lint}
Runs @file{scripts/lint.el} over every @file{lisp/*.el}: checkdoc on
each file and package-lint when it is installed.  Any finding is fatal.
CI runs the same command (@file{scripts/lint.sh}) on one Emacs version,
because checkdoc's rules differ across versions.
@item @command{make check-doc-drift}
Regenerates the three reference tables in @file{doc/generated/} into a
scratch directory and fails when they differ from the tracked copies.
The tracked tables are the artifact a clean checkout builds from;
@command{make regen-doc-tables} refreshes them after a keymap or command
change (@pxref{Generated Reference Tables}).
@end table

@noindent
@command{make check} includes @command{make check-doc-drift}, and the ERT
suite's @code{gascity-test-manual-key-registry-coverage} fails when a
registered view, key or agent verb is missing from @ref{View and Key
Reference}.  The full gate, from a clean checkout, is:

@example
./autogen.sh && ./configure --with-beads-dir="$HOME/workspace/beads.el"
make && make check && make lint
@end example

@node Regenerating the screenshots
@section Regenerating the screenshots

@cindex screenshots
@cindex pipeline
The screenshots are produced by a reusable pipeline under
@file{doc/screenshots}, so a sibling package can adopt it unchanged:

@table @file
@item screenshot.el
The package-agnostic capture engine: it strips the frame chrome, loads a
theme, waits for a view's asynchronous data, fits the frame to the
rendered content, and exports a PNG with @code{x-export-frames}.
@item gascity-shots.el
The gascity-specific half: it puts gascity.el and beads.el on the load
path and defines one shot per view.
@item capture.sh
The orchestrator: it runs a @emph{private}, headless Wayland compositor so
capture frames never appear on your desktop, runs Emacs once per theme,
and compresses each raw PNG to a small palette image plus a thumbnail
under @file{doc/images}.
@end table

@example
make screenshots     # or: doc/screenshots/capture.sh
@end example

@noindent
@code{capture.sh} resolves the repository root with @command{git rev-parse
--show-toplevel} (falling back to the script's parent-parent), so the target
works from the build tree as well as from a checkout.  This is a
@emph{local/graphical} target: it starts a private headless compositor and
needs a graphical Emacs, @command{sway} (a wlroots headless compositor),
ImageMagick @command{convert}, a running city, and the @code{ef-themes}
package, so continuous integration never runs it --- the committed images
under @file{doc/images} are the shipped artifact.
@file{doc/screenshots/README.md} documents the configuration variables and how
to reuse the engine.

